them back to the  the main base area and then you can dry  the fish and then produce fruit out of  that the and then the other thing is the  scavenger boats which will then able to  take three times the amount of scavenge  out of the water which would be the the  wood or the plastic once you get those  objects you bring them back into the  town you end up then putting bring them  in and then you can work with them that  way the plastic looks to be that it's  mostly for building the main part it's  like the main building block with the  wood but the wood is wet which means you  have to dry it first so once you dry it  you can then end up putting it into a  mechanic's area which would then it be  able to break down the wood and then  make firewood out of it or rope or  whatever you're looking to do with it  now over time you'll you're gonna use  those scavenger boats to go to  observation areas those observation  areas will then end up giving you  multiple different options of things to  do you'll be able to either get more  villagers you'll be able to save animals  you'll be able to get certain resources  or you'll get bonuses and resources like  extra water and then you'll also be able  to get things like oil now the oil will  allow you to go to different maps after  you can either do it from the oil or  with a mast so you can either do one or  the other now just take a step back one  of the things you get is you can also  get this water which is you know  refreshed water so the water itself is  then taken and then it's end up being  cleaned and then able to be drinkable  now you can end up doing that by using a  distiller which will end up burning the  salt water to be able to to drink from  it or you can route you can use research  points which you find on the islands to  be able to then upgrade different types  of things whereas with the water they  have a solar distilling area or the food  area which you can end up then using to  then catch fish randomly on this off the  side of your of the side of your your  your town which is really really neat  now I played this for about three and a  half hours there was very minimal  breakdown in what it was because it is  early access there were a little quirks  here and there which is you know what is  expected but it played very beautifully  the animations were fluid and great the  graphics of it was was fantastic I  wanted to keep playing it over and over  and over again because I thought that  the game ended up having this replay  value of it now the reason why I'm  saying it's got this replay value is  because when you go from zone to zone to  zone you'll end up getting the different  types of quote-unquote events which is  getting the villagers or the people or  I'm sorry the animals or the oil and  things like that  and to do that you need the oil or you  need a mast for your for your boat so  you have those two options but you  consistently can keep going going and  going and once you go to the end it  restarts the whole things you can you  take a different track if you want to  see what else you can get now what I  found interesting is that the it has a  very rimworld ish type mechanic where  you can tell your what your citizens or  your people your villagers should be  able to do specific jobs so what I ended  up doing was I ended up having one  person on the boat essentially making  sure he all he does is cut the wood end  up working on the  the mechanic shed and then I end up  having him do that and then they had  another person specifically working on  distilling the water and then I had  another person that was specifically  moving supplies and also putting things  into the drying racks and taking things  out of the drying racks and then I had  two people  I'm sorry not two people one person  specifically taking all of the the boats  out and being able to fill up the boats  bring him back into the dock once they  brought back into the dock then they  would just hop into another boat go out  so that it almost was like that person  was always working and then the person  that was hauling all the stuff around  he was ending up being constantly  working because he was just going onto  the boats taking the stuff off the boats  and bring them in so you had kind of  this fluid rounding motion of the game  so all my people consistently is went  non-stop now each of the villagers have  different stats on them so they have  fins so some of them can swim faster  than others some of the villagers end up  having you know they require less food  than others some require more water than  others and so each villager has their  own little needs and wants also and each  of your villagers they need the water  they need food they need sleep and they  also have the regular health bar so once  the health bar deteriorates which did  happen for me so one of them  deteriorated and disappeared and when  that ended up happening the  deterioration went away and I actually  ended up losing one of the one of my  villagers and you know yeah a really  interesting like almost like a floating  tombstone where he died and it was kind  of a little gruesome I was just like oh  no I did but you know it happened so we  kind of have to deal with that if you  will I tried this game twice the first  run which is most of the gameplay I have  was flawlessly done  to the to a really good point and I  wanted to see if I could take the  knowledge of the original first run into  the second run to see if I can make it  even better and faster and see if I can  end up making them builds correctly or  build differently or my build orders  because then I learned how to do certain  things more efficiently for instance I  didn't realize that there was a way to  research the items until about halfway  through so once I started learning how  to do that part of the game it ended up  working out pretty nicely so my second  run I was able to get to the crafting of  the the solar water distiller is way  faster and I was able to start working  on getting the the food the kelp fishing  lines and all that weight earlier also  which ended up working out pretty well  so it definitely makes you think and  makes you more efficient now I'm not  sure if they're planning on putting in a  hard mode or a different modes like  rimworld does like Rimmer all day in the  pudding you know they give you five  people right from start and you taste  they figure it out but they also have  like one mode that's like you have  nothing and you have to figure out what  you're doing from scratch so I wonder if  they're gonna ever implement that or be  like okay with one villager see how it  will see how it works so I would really  would love to see what what the pajama  llamas are going to end up doing with  this game to see how to make it more  complicated I do know that when I did  speak to them at PAX East they ended up  telling me that they were gonna be  putting in other things like  environmental environmental problems  because they got really really cool  whales that are floating around but they  said that they were thinking about  putting things in like dolphins and  sharks and things to kind of mess up  your ecosystem so that you can it makes  you think more than just having your  guys just jump in the water and go so  it'll be really interesting to see where  they're gonna end up taking taking the  scheme to the next level and DLCs and  maybe I'll end up having helicopter soon  and you'll be able to do grab things  that way or maybe that you'll end up  getting you know some type of larger  gameplay so I'm very excited to see it  so I would tell everyone if you want a  game you could just kind of veg out and  not think about go pick it up it is on  early access on the 26th of September we  got like I said we got this key front  and directly from from pajama llamas and  I thank them very much for doing this  because I was watching this game  throughout the whole year and I could  not wait to get my hands on it and it  did not disappoint and I'm very happy  that we were able to do this for them so  thank you very much for sitting through  and watching this review my name is now  though  also known as Lord Pete or PD or  whatever you'd like to call me on the  iron Lords podcast team now iron Lords  podcast is on Sundays at eleven o'clock  Eastern Time a.m. football season time  and then one o'clock on football season  and I would greatly appreciate it so  thank you very much everybody and have a  great day everybody  you  you  you  [Music]

